DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair 
 and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHA
 NGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal 
 are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/
 1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP
  for Candy Cane: Russian Candy Cane — Costume (you provide): Pink Seam
 less Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes *Da
 ncers of Color may wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeup: Full Stage Mak
 eup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Prop (BA provides): H
 oop\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and 
 powder matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire
  eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown ey
 e shadow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply m
 ascara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply e
 yeliner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply 
 plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• 
  Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow penci
 l (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstic
 k\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet sho
 es.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care w
 hile changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly no
 tify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of disc
 overy\, no matter how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or acces
 sories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  
 Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attem
 pt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• 
  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care
  to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• 
  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• 
  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not h
 andle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception 
 of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing ro
 oms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure he
 ad pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return all headpieces to
  their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to B
 allet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paint
 s\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
