 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · 9:00 PM–9:30 PM · Robinson Center\nMANDATO
 RY — production week. BA: Call Time is the time dancers should be chec
 k-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nIn Performance
  Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is name
 d. SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails a
 nd the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.co
 m/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUM
 E / HAIR / MAKEUP for Candy Cane: Russian Candy Cane — Costume (you pr
 ovide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink
  Ballet Shoes *Dancers of Color may wear flesh-tone ballet shoes\; Makeu
 p: Full Stage Makeup - Mascara Only OK\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Prop
  (BA provides): Hoop\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Appl
 y foundation and powder matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye s
 hadow over entire eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• 
  Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyela
 shes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before application of fake lashe
 s)\n•  Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks
  (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the sta
 ge lights)\n•  Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• 
  Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red
  or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and f
 lesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costum
 e pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\
 n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage 
 at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•  Never thr
 ow costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elas
 tic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n
 •  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume 
 or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and sha
 ll take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during it
 s removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne whil
 e in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member
 \n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costume\, w
 ith the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes from their as
 signed dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins
  used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return
  all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any an
 d all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pa
 ck markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stai
 n costumes.
